Subject: [ZEROX 6/6] Preserve real gameplay and plugin execution semantics

ZEROX v4 makes optimization non-destructive by default.

Default behavior:

- synchronous Bukkit tasks are measured and reported but are not skipped, cancelled, reordered, replaced, or deferred;
- Bukkit event listeners, commands, inventory actions, entity operations, world mutations, redstone, AI and plugin return values remain authoritative and synchronous;
- primed TNT uses Paper's upstream tick ceiling and normal fuse timing;
- the ZEROX TNT load-shedding limiter is disabled;
- armor-stand collision lookups and block-update pathfinding retain upstream behavior;
- Paper's optimized explosion calculation remains enabled;
- plugins that already request asynchronous scheduling use the bounded ZEROX parallel executor.

Master setting:

```properties
behavior.preserve-semantics=true
```

This master setting overrides older v3 values that enabled task or TNT deferral. Therefore, an upgraded installation preserves real behavior even when its existing configuration still contains:

```properties
plugins.defer-repeating-tasks=true
tnt.load-shedding-enabled=true
```

Optional emergency load shedding can only be enabled deliberately:

```properties
behavior.preserve-semantics=false
plugins.defer-repeating-tasks=true
tnt.load-shedding-enabled=true
```

That optional mode changes timing and is not the v4 default.

Safe parallelism boundary:

- existing Bukkit async tasks: parallel and bounded;
- Paper chunk workers, I/O and Netty: parallel;
- synchronous world/event/plugin behavior: unchanged;
- arbitrary synchronous callbacks are never moved to worker threads automatically.
